{
  "name": "Update living docs on task completion",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "When a spec task finishes, refresh PROJECT-STATE.md so the living-state doc tracks progress (Requirement 5.1): the machine-managed STATE block plus any prose section the completed task made stale. The general 'any change' coverage is handled by the keep-project-state-live Stop hook; this one fires precisely at spec-task boundaries. Research-log verdicts remain auto-appended by the in-code Living-Docs Writer when the kill-gate runs.",
  "when": {
    "type": "postTaskExecution"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A spec task just completed. Update PROJECT-STATE.md so it stays a true live picture of the project.\n\nRules:\n- Machine-managed STATE block: edit ONLY the lines between '<!-- BEGIN STATE -->' and '<!-- END STATE -->'. Keep the exact three-line format the Living-Docs Writer uses: '- **Phase:**', '- **Updated:**' (today's date, YYYY-MM-DD), and '- **Summary:**'.\n- Prose outside the markers (Spec completion status table, Strategic decisions, Obstacles / open risks, Immediate next steps, etc.): update the sections this task affected — tick/retire a closed item, add a decision bullet, correct anything now stale. Preserve all markers and unrelated prose verbatim.\n- Determine current phase/summary from the spec tasks.md files under .kiro/specs/ (which tasks are [x]) and the task that just completed. Be concise and strictly factual; do not invent progress not reflected in specs or code; distinguish locally-verified work from live-cloud claims.\n- Never write any secret value, key, token, or JWT into the file. Reference credentials by name only.\n- Do not touch LESSONS.md (hand-authored constraints). Kill-gate verdicts go to RESEARCH-LOG.md via the Living-Docs Writer append path, never into PROJECT-STATE.md.\n- Make the edits and stop; do not run builds or commit."
  }
}
